Michael Lewis's latest book flash boys  sets its sights on the world of  high-frequency trading that complex  arcane practice only performed by the  most sophisticated investors armed with  the most powerful computers except  actually it isn't all that complex at  all it was a major plot point of  Superman 3 remember Superman 3 it's the  crappy one with Richard Pryor in it  Pryor's character engages in a little  fiduciary malfeasance commonly known as  salami slicing here's how it works  an employee's paycheck is always rounded  down to the nearest percent which of  course raises the question where do all  those functional scents go what priors  character does is take all of those  little fractional cents leftover from  each transaction and deposit them into  his own secret account in each case the  individual theft is very small but in  the aggregate it Nets him a ton of cash  Oh  now in many ways this is a lot like what  high frequency traders do they buy  stocks just before other people do and  then resell them at a small increase  pocketing the tiny profit like priors  paycheck Scheme each transaction is so  microscopic that no individual would  ever notice or care what was going on  but over thousands or millions of trades  it really begins to add up all you need  is a very high-speed data connection and  a computer just like Richard Pryor
 

